{"Title":"An Act relative to the automatic renewal of professional licenses","BillNumber":"S203","DocketNumber":"SD1065","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PMO","Name":"Patrick M. O'Connor","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PMO","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T20:07:40.047"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PMO","Name":"Patrick M. O'Connor","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PMO","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T20:07:40.0466667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S203/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. O'Connor, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 203) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation relative to the automatic renewal of professional licenses.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding any license renewal application set forth in Chapter 112 of the general laws, the division of professional licensure shall develop and implement an automatic license renewal system for the professional licenses set forth in this chapter. The automatic license renewal system shall be designed to notify licensed professionals of an upcoming license expiration date and offer the ability to automatically renew the license online, wherever possible.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This Act shall take effect immediately upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}